     A(\xi) u_1(x) + B(\xi) u_2(x) & \text{for } x < \xi \\
     C(\xi) u_1(x) + D(\xi) u_2(x) & \text{for } x > \xi
     \end{cases}
     \]
   - Ensure continuity at \( x = \xi \):
     \[
     A(\xi) u_1(\xi) + B(\xi) u_2(\xi) = C(\xi) u_1(\xi) + D(\xi) u_2(\xi)
     \]
   - Ensure the jump condition in the first derivative:
     \[
     \left. \frac{dG}{dx} \right|_{x=\xi^+} - \left. \frac{dG}{dx} \right|_{x=\xi^-} = 1
     \]

3. **Apply Boundary Conditions:**
   - Use \( G(0, \xi) = 0 \) and \( G(1, \xi) = .0 \) to determine the coefficients \( A(\xi) \), \( B(\xi) \), \( C(\xi) \), and \( D(\xi) \).

